{
  "answer": "The record indicates Bea and Arun are not on the same page. Bea believes Arun knows the flute is playback, but Arun says he does not know whether it is live and only saw the lobby screen. Jules's 18:05 remark accurately reports Bea's expressed belief, but it does not confirm Arun's knowledge; the source shows Arun explicitly denying such knowledge.",
  "source_citations": [
    {
      "source_id": "flute-observer-record",
      "version": 1,
      "quote": "At 18:00, Bea and Jules read the facilitator tablet. It said, \"For tonight's demonstration, the flute audio is a prerecorded track.\" The lobby monitor, visible from Arun's seat, displayed only \"Restoration demonstration.\" The facilitator tablet faced away from Arun, who stayed in his seat throughout this period."
    },
    {
      "source_id": "flute-observer-record",
      "version": 1,
      "quote": "Bea pointed toward Arun and told Jules, \"Arun knows the flute is playback. He watched the whole briefing.\" Bea had seen Arun looking at the lobby monitor; she had not checked which information it displayed. Jules heard her, but Arun was too far away to hear this exchange."
    },
    {
      "source_id": "flute-observer-record",
      "version": 1,
      "quote": "Arun then told Jules, \"I saw the lobby screen, not that tablet. I still don't know whether the flute we're about to hear is live.\" Jules heard him. Bea was outside and did not hear him."
    },
    {
      "source_id": "flute-observer-record",
      "version": 1,
      "quote": "At 18:05, Jules told the director, \"Bea thinks Arun knows that tonight's flute is playback.\" Arun and Bea were not present for this last conversation."
    }
  ],
  "uncertainty": "The source is an observer record for a fictional demonstration and reports statements without verifying private mental states or equipment. Bea's belief is based on the unchecked assumption that Arun saw the full briefing; Arun's denial is also only a reported statement. The actual truth about the flute audio cannot be confirmed from this record.",
  "assumptions": "We assume that the statements are reported accurately by the observer and that 'on the same page' means sharing knowledge about whether the flute audio is playback. We do not assume that reported expressions directly reveal private beliefs or world facts."
}
